    "text": "A silicon specimen is made into a <math><mi>p</mi></math>-type semiconductor by doping, on an average, one indium atom per <math><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math> silicon atoms. If the number density of atoms in the silicon specimen is <math><msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>28</mn></mrow></msup></math> atoms <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the number of acceptor atoms in silicon per cubic centimetre will be",
